# @req REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
"""
# One selector identity for both advice families

## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Prove that a pointcut has exactly one identity, the `PointcutSelectorId` produced by `pointcut_selector_parse_v1`, whether it is written as a logical-family selector or as a mir-family predicate.
Audience: compiler engineers who maintain aspect matching, the aspect cache
keys and the reverse-reference tables.

Lifecycle: research doc/01_research/domain/dir_tldr_aspect.md; plan
doc/03_plan/compiler/aspect_cache/aspect_tldr_async_trace_plan.md (stage AW-3);
architecture doc/04_architecture/extreme_typing_traceability.md; design
doc/05_design/compiler/cache/aspect_tldr_async_trace.md (section 3, gap G11).

## What the operator can rely on
A mir-family predicate (`on pc{...}` advice) is lowered into the shard selector
by `aop_predicate_lower_v1`. Lowering either gives a selector that matches
exactly the functions the mir matcher (`match_advice_for_join_point`, the
matcher `weave_function` uses) matches, or it gives `supported = false`. An
unsupported predicate is never cached; it still has a stable digest so that
its consumers can be named.

| mir predicate | lowered selector | why |
|---|---|---|
| `execution(* run(..))`, `run` | `execution(run)` | exact function name |
| `execution(* run_*(..))`, `run_*` | `execution(run_*)` | prefix glob |
| `@inline` | `attr(inline)` | attribute membership |
| `!`, `&`, `|`, `( )` | unchanged | same precedence in both grammars |
| `*`, `execution(* *(..))`, `*_run`, `a*b` | unsupported | no match-all, suffix or infix atom |
| `execution(* app.run(..))` | unsupported | dotted names are not shard symbols |
| `module:...`, `effect:...`, `join:...` | unsupported | facts carry no such field |
| `execution(run)`, `execution(* run)` | unsupported | the mir matcher never matches them |
| `attr(x)`, `within(x)` as selector calls | unsupported | the mir matcher never matches them |

Equality with the mir matcher is stated for `forward` join-point facts whose
`symbol` is the function name and whose `attrs` are its attributes.

## Match identity is not order identity
The selector id says which functions a predicate matches, nothing more. The mir
matcher also ranks equal-priority advice by `predicate_specificity`, which is
read from the spelling: `execution(* run(..))` ranks 1 (it contains a `*`),
`execution(i64 run())` and `run` rank 4, and a `*` in a trailing comment lowers
the rank to 1 as well. These spellings share one selector id and can still be
woven in a different order. `aop_predicate_specificity_v1` returns that rank;
every key that covers woven order (the mdsoc selection key, the mir rule set
digest of the weave plan) folds it next to the selector id.

## Retired identity
`aop_selector_digest` and its substring read-set are deleted. The mdsoc
selection key folds `aop_selector_id_v1` with the specificity; the reverse index
uses the selector id, and its read-set is derived from the atoms of the lowered
selector. The example below reads the file that defined the retired digest and
the file that called it. That no other caller is left under `src`, `test` and
`scripts` is the `git grep` evidence recorded with the change, not something
this spec scans for.

## Decision inventory (aop_selector_identity_v1.spl)

| Decision | Conditions | Covering examples |
|---|---|---|
| name is empty | c1 | empty predicate / every named predicate |
| character is an identifier character | lower, upper, digit, underscore ranges | `Run_2`, `a.b`, `a{b`, `a:b` |
| glob is an identifier | c1 | `run` / `run*` |
| glob ends with `*` | c1 | `run*` / `a.b` |
| prefix is an identifier | c1 | `run*` / `*` |
| call-end scan: in range and depth open | c1, c2 | call ends the predicate (`execution(* run(..))`) / an operator follows the call |
| token opens / closes a group | c1 / c1 | nested argument lists |
| name scan: before call end and not `(` | c1, c2 | `execution(* run)` / `execution(* run(..))` |
| token is an operator or a parenthesis | five alternatives | `!`, `&`, `|`, `(`, `)` examples |
| selector call is not `execution` | c1 | `attr(inline)` / `execution(...)` |
| execution atom is not expressible | c1 | `execution(* *(..))` / `execution(* run(..))` |
| predicate starts with `@` | c1 | `@inline` / `run` |
| attribute name is an identifier | c1 | `@inline` / `@name(x)` |
| `module:` or `effect:` form | c1, c2 | `module:app.*`, `effect:io`, `run` |
| predicate has a selector call | c1 | `execution(...)` / `run` |
| token stream validates | c1 | `execution(* run(..))` / `execution(* run(..)) &` |
| nothing was lowered | c1 | every unsupported / supported pair |
"""

# @manual: primary
# @tag:unit
# @tag:compiler
# @tag:aop
# @tag:cache

use std.spec.*
use std.io.{file_read}
use compiler.frontend.core.aop.{JoinPoint, JoinPointContext, JoinPointKind, WeavingConfig,
    WeavingRule, AdviceForm, match_advice_for_join_point}
use compiler.common.cache_contract.aspect_match_shard_v1.{JoinPointFactV1,
    directory_join_point_facts_v1, pointcut_selector_parse_v1, pointcut_match_shard_compute_v1}
use compiler.frontend.core.aop_selector_identity_v1.{aop_predicate_lower_v1, aop_selector_id_v1,
    aop_predicate_specificity_v1}

struct ProbeFn:
    name: text
    attrs: [text]

fn probe_functions() -> [ProbeFn]:
    [ProbeFn(name: "run", attrs: []),
     ProbeFn(name: "run_fast", attrs: ["inline"]),
     ProbeFn(name: "run_2", attrs: ["hot", "inline"]),
     ProbeFn(name: "Run_2", attrs: []),
     ProbeFn(name: "app_run", attrs: ["hot"]),
     ProbeFn(name: "stop", attrs: ["inline"]),
     ProbeFn(name: "execution", attrs: []),
     ProbeFn(name: "inline", attrs: [])]

# The mir matcher: one rule, one execution join point, exactly as weave_function asks.
fn mir_matches(predicate: text, probe: ProbeFn) -> bool:
    val context = JoinPointContext(function_name: probe.name, module_path: "app.core",
        signature: "* {probe.name}(...)", attributes: probe.attrs, effects: ["io"])
    val join_point = JoinPoint(JoinPointKind.Execution, probe.name, context.signature, "", "", 0, 0, context)
    val config = WeavingConfig.from_rules([WeavingRule(predicate_text: predicate,
        advice_function: "advice", form: AdviceForm.Before, priority: 1)])
    match_advice_for_join_point(config, join_point).matched.len() == 1

# The mir matcher with two equal-priority rules on one execution join point:
# advice `m` under `first`, advice `z` under `second`. Returns the woven order.
fn mir_order(first: text, second: text, probe: ProbeFn) -> text:
    val context = JoinPointContext(function_name: probe.name, module_path: "app.core",
        signature: "* {probe.name}(...)", attributes: probe.attrs, effects: ["io"])
    val join_point = JoinPoint(JoinPointKind.Execution, probe.name, context.signature, "", "", 0, 0, context)
    val config = WeavingConfig.from_rules([
        WeavingRule(predicate_text: first, advice_function: "m", form: AdviceForm.Before, priority: 1),
        WeavingRule(predicate_text: second, advice_function: "z", form: AdviceForm.Before, priority: 1)])
    var names: [text] = []
    for matched in match_advice_for_join_point(config, join_point).matched:
        names.push(matched.advice_function)
    names.join(",")

# Every (predicate, function) pair whose woven order against the rank-2 rule
# `@inline` is not the order its specificity predicts: a higher rank goes first,
# an equal or lower rank goes after `m`.
fn order_mismatches(predicates: [text]) -> [text]:
    var out: [text] = []
    for predicate in predicates:
        for probe in probe_functions():
            if probe.attrs.contains("inline") and mir_matches(predicate, probe):
                var expected = "m,z"
                if aop_predicate_specificity_v1(predicate) > aop_predicate_specificity_v1("@inline"):
                    expected = "z,m"
                if mir_order("@inline", predicate, probe) != expected:
                    out.push("{predicate} on {probe.name}")
    out

# The shard matcher over the one forward fact of the same function.
fn shard_matches(predicate: text, probe: ProbeFn) -> bool:
    val fact = JoinPointFactV1(id: "app/core.spl::{probe.name}", kind: "forward", symbol: probe.name,
        attrs: probe.attrs, owner_file: "app/core.spl", base_body_digest: "")
    val facts = directory_join_point_facts_v1("app", ["app/core.spl"], [fact], [], true)
    pointcut_match_shard_compute_v1(aop_predicate_lower_v1(predicate), facts).sorted_matching_ids.len() == 1

# Every (predicate, function) pair on which the two matchers disagree.
fn disagreements(predicates: [text]) -> [text]:
    var out: [text] = []
    for predicate in predicates:
        for probe in probe_functions():
            if mir_matches(predicate, probe) != shard_matches(predicate, probe):
                out.push("{predicate} on {probe.name}")
    out

# Predicates of the list whose lowering is supported.
fn supported_of(predicates: [text]) -> [text]:
    var out: [text] = []
    for predicate in predicates:
        if aop_predicate_lower_v1(predicate).supported: out.push(predicate)
    out

fn expressible_corpus() -> [text]:
    ["execution(* run(..))",
     "execution ( * run ( .. ) )",
     "execution(i64 run())",
     "execution(* Run_2(a, (b)))",
     "execution(* run_*(..))",
     "run",
     "  run_fast  ",
     "run*",
     "@inline",
     "  @hot ",
     "execution(* run(..)) | execution(* stop(..))",
     "execution(* run*(..)) & !execution(* run_fast(..))",
     "!(execution(* run(..)) | execution(* stop(..)))",
     "execution(* run(..)) # trailing note\n",
     "execution(* execution(..))"]

fn inexpressible_corpus() -> [text]:
    ["*",
     "",
     "execution(* *(..))",
     "execution(* *_run(..))",
     "*_run",
     "a*b",
     "a.b",
     "a\{b",
     "a:b",
     "execution(* app.run(..))",
     "module:app.*",
     "effect:io",
     "join:execution",
     "execution(run)",
     "execution(* run)",
     "attr(inline)",
     "!attr(inline)",
     "within(app.core)",
     "execution(* run(..)) & attr(inline)",
     "@name(x)",
     "@",
     "execution(* run(..)) &",
     "get(run)",
     "mystery()"]

describe "Lowering a mir-family predicate into the shard selector":
    it "lowers every expressible predicate and matches exactly what the mir matcher matches":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Lower each expressible predicate and compare both matchers on every probe function")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(supported_of(expressible_corpus())).to_equal(expressible_corpus())
        expect(disagreements(expressible_corpus())).to_equal([])

    it "selects the functions the mir matcher selects, not merely the same count":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Pin concrete match results so that agreement cannot be vacuous")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val run = ProbeFn(name: "run", attrs: [])
        val fast = ProbeFn(name: "run_fast", attrs: ["inline"])
        expect(mir_matches("execution(* run(..))", run)).to_equal(true)
        expect(shard_matches("execution(* run(..))", run)).to_equal(true)
        expect(shard_matches("execution(* run(..))", fast)).to_equal(false)
        expect(shard_matches("execution(* run*(..)) & !execution(* run_fast(..))", fast)).to_equal(false)
        expect(shard_matches("execution(* run*(..)) & !execution(* run_fast(..))", run)).to_equal(true)
        expect(shard_matches("@inline", fast)).to_equal(true)
        expect(shard_matches("@inline", run)).to_equal(false)

    it "marks every predicate without an equivalent shard atom unsupported":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Lower each inexpressible predicate and require supported = false")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(supported_of(inexpressible_corpus())).to_equal([])

    it "never claims a match for an unsupported predicate, so it cannot skip a weave":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("An unsupported selector matches nothing in a shard even where the mir matcher matches")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val run = ProbeFn(name: "run", attrs: [])
        expect(mir_matches("*", run)).to_equal(true)
        expect(shard_matches("*", run)).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_predicate_lower_v1("*").needs_universe).to_equal(true)

    it "does not read attr() or within() selector calls as shard atoms":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("The mir matcher never matches these calls; passing them through would match")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val fast = ProbeFn(name: "run_fast", attrs: ["inline"])
        expect(mir_matches("attr(inline)", fast)).to_equal(false)
        expect(pointcut_selector_parse_v1("attr(inline)").supported).to_equal(true)
        expect(aop_predicate_lower_v1("attr(inline)").supported).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_predicate_lower_v1("execution(run_fast)").supported).to_equal(false)

describe "Equivalent spellings share one PointcutSelectorId":
    it "gives match-equivalent mir spellings of one function the logical selector digest":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Compare the ids of four spellings with the logical-family selector digest")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val logical = pointcut_selector_parse_v1("execution(run)").selector_digest
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* run(..))")).to_equal(logical)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution ( * run ( .. ) )")).to_equal(logical)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(i64 run()) # note\n")).to_equal(logical)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("  run ")).to_equal(logical)
        expect(logical.starts_with("sha256:")).to_equal(true)

    it "gives prefix and attribute predicates the logical selector's digest":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Compare prefix and attribute spellings with their logical selectors")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("run_*")).to_equal(pointcut_selector_parse_v1("execution(run_*)").selector_digest)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* run_*(..))")).to_equal(aop_selector_id_v1("run_*"))
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("@inline")).to_equal(pointcut_selector_parse_v1("attr(inline)").selector_digest)

    it "keeps different selectors apart":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Different names, forms and operators give different ids")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("run") == aop_selector_id_v1("stop")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("run") == aop_selector_id_v1("run*")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("run") == aop_selector_id_v1("@run")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* a(..)) & execution(* b(..))") ==
            aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* a(..)) | execution(* b(..))")).to_equal(false)

    it "shares one digest between token respellings of an unsupported predicate":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Whitespace and comments do not split an unsupported token-form predicate")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* app.run(..))")).to_equal(aop_selector_id_v1("execution ( * app . run ( .. ) )"))
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* app.run(..)) # note\n")).to_equal(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* app.run(..))"))
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("  module:app.*  ")).to_equal(aop_selector_id_v1("module:app.*"))

    it "keeps unsupported predicates with different match text apart":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("The mir matcher compares these texts exactly, so their ids must differ")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("@name(x)#first") == aop_selector_id_v1("@name(x)#second")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("module:app(x)#first") == aop_selector_id_v1("module:app(x)#second")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("effect:io(x)#first") == aop_selector_id_v1("effect:io(x)#second")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("module:app.*") == aop_selector_id_v1("effect:app.*")).to_equal(false)
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* app.run(..))") == aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* app.stop(..))")).to_equal(false)

describe "Selector identity does not cover weave order":
    it "lets a respelling with the same selector id flip equal-priority advice":
        # @capture(exec): selector ids and woven order of both spellings
        step("Weave two equal-priority rules on run, with the first rule spelled with and without a star")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val run = ProbeFn(name: "run", attrs: [])
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(* run(..))")).to_equal(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(i64 run())"))
        expect(mir_order("execution(* run(..))", "run", run)).to_equal("z,m")
        expect(mir_order("execution(i64 run())", "run", run)).to_equal("m,z")

    it "reports the rank that decides that order, also for a star in a trailing comment":
        # @capture(exec): specificity of each spelling and the woven order
        step("Read the specificity of four spellings of one selector and weave the commented one")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val run = ProbeFn(name: "run", attrs: [])
        expect(aop_predicate_specificity_v1("execution(* run(..))")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 - the spelling contains a star
        expect(aop_predicate_specificity_v1("execution(i64 run())")).to_equal(4)  # oracle: 4 - exact spelling without a star
        expect(aop_predicate_specificity_v1("run")).to_equal(4)  # oracle: 4 - exact spelling without a star
        expect(aop_predicate_specificity_v1("execution(i64 run()) # *")).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 - the star is in the comment
        expect(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(i64 run()) # *")).to_equal(aop_selector_id_v1("execution(i64 run())"))
        expect(mir_order("execution(i64 run()) # *", "run", run)).to_equal("z,m")

    it "orders every expressible predicate as its specificity predicts":
        # @capture(exec): predicates whose woven order differs from the predicted one
        step("Weave each expressible predicate against an equal-priority attribute rule on every probe function")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        expect(order_mismatches(expressible_corpus())).to_equal([])
        expect(mir_order("@inline", "run_fast", ProbeFn(name: "run_fast", attrs: ["inline"]))).to_equal("z,m")
        expect(mir_order("@inline", "run*", ProbeFn(name: "run_fast", attrs: ["inline"]))).to_equal("m,z")

describe "The retired selector digest":
    it "is gone from the file that defined it and from the file that called it":
        # @capture(exec): the compared match results and digests
        step("Read the former defining file and the former calling file and require the retired name to be absent")
        # @req: REQ-ASPECT-AW3-SELECTOR-IDENTITY
        val keys = file_read("src/compiler/85.mdsoc/aop_cache/aop_group_keys.spl") ?? ""
        val index = file_read("src/compiler/85.mdsoc/aop_index/reverse_index.spl") ?? ""
        expect(keys.contains("aop_selector_id_v1(predicate_text)")).to_equal(true)
        expect(index.contains("aop_predicate_lower_v1(rule.predicate_text)")).to_equal(true)
        expect(keys.contains("aop_selector_digest")).to_equal(false)
        expect(index.contains("aop_selector_digest")).to_equal(false)
        expect(index.contains("predicate_text.contains(")).to_equal(false)
